'local-guide':()=>modal('Intelligence, close to home',`<div class="stack"><div><h3>Computer · Ollama</h3><p>1. Install from <a href="https://ollama.com/download" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ollama.com</a>.<br>2. Run <code>ollama pull llama3.2</code>.<br>3. Allow your BookWiz origin with OLLAMA_ORIGINS and start Ollama.<br>4. Add an Ollama connection in the hub. Use <code>http://localhost:11434/v1</code>.</p></div><div><h3>Computer · LM Studio & GGUF</h3><p>Install <a href="https://lmstudio.ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LM Studio</a>, import or download a compatible GGUF file, load it, and start its OpenAI-compatible local server. Enable CORS. Enter its served model ID in BookWiz. Large models need sufficient memory.</p></div><div><h3>iPhone & iPad</h3><p>In the installed BookWiz app, choose Apple Intelligence in the hub. Enable it in device Settings, finish model downloads and use a supported language on a compatible iPhone or iPad with iOS 26 or later. See <a href="https://support.apple.com/121115" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Apple’s availability guide</a>. No API key is needed. In a browser, use a compatible local service through Custom endpoint instead.</p></div><div><h3>Android</h3><p><a href="https://ai.google.dev/edge" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google AI Edge</a> and compatible native runtimes can run supported models on eligible devices. Import model files into a compatible runtime, then connect its local API. Connect an installed OpenAI-compatible local runtime where available.</p></div><div><h3>Importing model files</h3><p>Download models from trusted publishers, check the model license and hardware requirements, and import the file into LM Studio or another compatible runtime. A GGUF, MLX, or task file is not interchangeable. BookWiz connects to the runtime; it does not upload model weights to a server.</p></div><p class="notice">Local inference can be free of per-token fees, but uses your device’s memory, storage, battery, and compute. Browser local-network restrictions may prevent hosted-to-local access.</p></div>`,B('close-dialog','Got it','','primary')),
